{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1487 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "70890391266f55cc19a0cc8611b3c907e318ac64db67f9f3fc0d8851e143b707" :edb/db-before-t 1486 :edb/db-after-t 1487 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534799 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:17:43.946Z" 13194139534799 true] [17592186096624 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310780 13194139534799 true] [17592186096624 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310794 13194139534799 true] [17592186096626 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310787 13194139534799 true] [17592186096626 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310801 13194139534799 true] [17592186096923 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534799 true] [17592186096923 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041157/assets/9eb2efa6d60dc4bd1d7915900e60be8a891f824799ed6ada8f2753fa71bb01c6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534799 true] [17592186096923 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1124/Source/Images/q-11793.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534799 false] [17592186096923 1145 "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(-2,2)$ and passes through the point $(6,10).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-2,2),$ we substitute $h=-2$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(6,10),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=10$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+2) \\\\ (10-2)^{2} & =4p(6+2) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+2) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(2)(x+2) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =8(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=2$ is positive." 13194139534799 true] [17592186310780 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310781 13194139534799 true] [17592186310780 1089 "q-115633" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310780 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534799 true] [17592186310780 1100 "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-2,-2).$" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310780 1113 #uuid "b24732f9-7b75-59b2-a18e-ce5ccd87f7dd" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310780 1145 "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,-2),$ we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-2)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310782 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310783 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310784 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310785 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310786 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1041 "selection" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310785 13194139534799 true] [17592186310781 1110 #uuid "3f30297e-01ec-5ead-8058-5f9754035dfa" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310782 1034 "{y}^{2}=4x" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534799 true] [17592186310782 1111 #uuid "222fe8d9-adb9-5edd-9390-b3f17d688162" 13194139534799 true] [17592186310783 1034 "{x}^{2}=2